---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import grahamPhoto from '../assets/graham.jpeg';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About" description="Senior Engineering Manager and tech lead with nearly 20 years in software, writing about AI, engineering craft, and leadership." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="intro">
				<Image src={grahamPhoto} alt="Graham Jackson" class="photo" width={120} height={120} />
				<p class="label">About</p>
			</div>

			<p>
				I'm Graham Jackson. Senior Engineering Manager and tech lead at a Fortune 500 company. Nearly 20 years in software, most of it spent building systems, leading teams, and making decisions with incomplete information.
			</p>

			<p>
				This is where I think out loud.
			</p>

			<p>
				I write about three things: <strong>AI and what it's actually doing to software development</strong>, the <strong>craft of engineering</strong> and what it means to build things well, and <strong>leadership</strong> when the ground keeps shifting.
			</p>

			<p>
				Not here to sell you optimism or pessimism. Just hot takes and other observations from someone in the middle of it.
			</p>

			<hr />

			<p class="personal">
				When he's not thinking about AI and engineering, Graham is watching hockey or being supervised by two Labrador Retrievers.
			</p>

		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	main {
		width: 720px;
		max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
		margin: auto;
		padding: 3em 1em;
	}
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}
	.photo {
		width: 80px;
		height: 80px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		object-fit: cover;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}
	.label {
		font-size: 0.65rem;
		color: var(--accent);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.15em;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.personal {
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.9em;
	}
</style>
